M9 ports native image content-part formats and MIME-routing behavior using
agent/image_routing.py, agent/anthropic_message_convert.py, and
agent/gemini_native_adapter.py as implementation references. Anima applies its
own scoped attachment records, bounded reads, model capability gating and
request-only hydration. The original upstream notice is retained below.

M16 source revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899 (verified clean files).
M16 adapts terminal structured-error-code preservation from
agent/codex_runtime.py::_on_terminal/_raise_stream_error and
agent/codex_responses_adapter.py::_format_responses_error. Anima intentionally
uses fixed whitelisted code/parameter diagnostics instead of reflecting raw
provider messages. Request/auth/endpoints remain unchanged; no Python runtime,
profiles or token files are imported. Official structured recovery categories
were checked against OpenAI Docs.

M23 source revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899.
M23 adapts the grouped removal of tools/tool_choice/parallel_tool_calls from
agent/chat_completion_helpers.py::_codex_summary_attempt. Anima applies this
request-shape rule whenever its ChatGPT adapter has no configured tools; prior
function-call/result input and ordinary toolful requests are preserved. This
does not copy Hermes' Chat Completions cache-prefix policy or introduce retries.

M26 source revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899.
M26 uses agent/turn_loop_errors.py::handle_outer_loop_error/OuterErrorVerdict
and agent/turn_retry_state.py::TurnRetryState as architectural references for
bounded phase-aware recovery. Native ChatGPT transport retries one explicitly
classified pre-stream gateway failure with the same authority and request;
ambiguous sends, terminal codes and stream failures remain terminal. Existing
API-provider stream retries now honor explicit zero. No upstream credential
refresh, payload repair, fallback or outer-loop retry framework is copied.

M48 source revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899.
M48 adapts the exact model-access rejection marker from
agent/error_classifier.py::CODEX_ACCOUNT_MODEL_ENTITLEMENT_MARKER/_classify_400,
with tests/agent/test_codex_model_entitlement_rotation.py as its source fixture.
Anima recognizes only bounded HTTP 400 top-level detail or detail.message with
absent/null code and absent/null or four recognized types. It emits one fixed
model-access explanation without provider/model text. No credential rotation,
fallback, retry, permission change or historical-failure diagnosis is copied.

M49 source revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899.
M49 adapts subscription catalog slug/visibility/priority ordering and exact-ID
deduplication intent from hermes_cli/codex_models.py::_ranked_slugs, including
